Each green phase lasts exactly green_duration ticks and alternates: north-south (N/S) green from tick 0 to tick green_duration - 1, then east-west (E/W) green from Green_duration to 2 * green_duration - 1, and so on. The car at tick t passes if and only if its direction is the one whose green phase covers t, and the function returns True or False accordingly. The previous light is always reset before inspecting the next event, which means a red event followed by a green one on the same lane is still counted correctly. A simple parity test on ticks of the form floor(t / green_duration) recovers the phase at each event tick. The parity is 0 for N/S and 1 for E/W.

