Each direction's green period has the same start and end, but their allowed zones inside it differ. North time runs from tick 0 to tick (green_duration + 1) // 2 - 1, wrapping the odd case, while south time starts at green_duration // 2. East and west use the same boundaries as north and south, since their phases alternate in step with theirs. A car outside its allowed zone refers to the other direction's green, which is why south and west look at the value at green_duration // 2. The code checks whether a car's tick lies inside its own green zone rather than its neighbour's.

